                StoryPart(2, "The Wall's History", listOf(
                    "The school archivist found photographs showing that the wall had once displayed a science timeline and later a painted map. Neither design had been preserved. The art teacher explained that the new mural should be durable, easy to maintain, and appropriate for students of different ages.",
                    "The club measured the wall with the facilities manager and checked which paint types were approved. Students were not allowed to climb ladders or prepare the surface themselves. The school would arrange the technical work and supervise the painting day."
