                StoryPart(3, "A Design with Room", listOf(
                    "The first design showed a large tree with a sentence on every leaf. Some students felt the words were too small, while others thought the design looked crowded. Nosa suggested using fewer words and larger symbols so the message could be understood from the corridor.",
                    "The art teacher helped the club make three mock-ups. Students voted on the layout, and the winning design used a tree whose branches held short promises about shared spaces. The words were general actions, not rules directed at particular people."
