                StoryPart(4, "Checking Every Word", listOf(
                    "Before painting, the club reviewed each phrase for clarity and tone. One suggestion sounded like a command to always be cheerful, so the students removed it. They agreed that a mural should encourage helpful actions without telling anyone how they must feel.",
                    "The final phrases included listening carefully, sharing credit, caring for common spaces, and asking for help when needed. The head teacher approved the design after the student council reviewed it. The school scheduled the work with the approved materials and supervision."
                )),
                StoryPart(5, "The Painting Day", listOf(
                    "A professional prepared the wall, and the art teacher supervised students as they painted approved sections at ground level. Staff handled any work requiring ladders or specialist equipment. Nosa helped fill the tree branches with colour and checked each phrase against the approved design.",
                    "The club worked in short shifts so the corridor remained clear. When one colour looked different after drying, the art teacher adjusted the plan using the manufacturer's guidance. The students learned that a mural required patience as much as creativity."
                )),
                StoryPart(6, "A Phrase Left Out", listOf(
                    "During the final review, a student noticed that a phrase had been copied incorrectly. The club checked the original idea board and corrected the wording before the wall was sealed. They also confirmed that no student's name or private message had been included without permission.",
                    "The head teacher asked the club to document the paint products and care instructions for future maintenance. Nosa placed the approved design and colour references in the art room folder. That record would help the school repair the mural without guessing later."
                )),
                StoryPart(7, "The Opening", listOf(
                    "At assembly, the art club introduced the mural and explained how the ideas had been collected. They thanked the students who contributed suggestions without naming anyone. The head teacher said the wall belonged to the whole school, so everyone could help keep the area clean and report damage.",
                    "Younger pupils read the phrases aloud and pointed to the painted leaves. One teacher suggested using the mural as a starting point for class discussions about cooperation. The art club welcomed the idea but made clear that the mural was not a test; students could interpret the phrases in their own way."
