                StoryPart(9, "The Promise Board", listOf(
                    "The student council proposed a rotating board beside the mural where classes could write one shared project goal each month. The head teacher approved a supervised trial. The goals were about school activities, such as organising a book swap or improving recycling signs, not promises about personal feelings or private lives.",
                    "The art club designed a simple template with a date and space for a class name. At the end of each month, the council would record what had been completed and what needed more time. The mural and board now worked together: one offered lasting ideas, while the other supported practical action."
